abstract: >-
  For identities built from shifted and twisted zeta and Dirichlet L factors with squarefull corrections,
  no identity detects primes modulo p, the divided count needs a factor of degree divisible by p exactly once,
  and the least degree yielding pi(x) mod p^k is S(p^ceil(k/2)) (signed) or S(p^k) (unsigned), S the Kempner
  function. pi(x) mod 3 below the square root is equivalent to D_3(x) mod 9 below the square root, and
  D_3(x) is computable in O(x^(5/9) log^2 x) operations, so pi(x) mod 3 is computable in x^(5/9+o(1)).
  Core statements are machine-checked in Lean 4. Prepared with Claude (Anthropic); several results were first
  proposed by ChatGPT (OpenAI) and independently checked. No external human referee has reviewed this work.
keywords:
